{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: E1 truncation can split a UTF-16 surrogate pair**

`truncateCheckRunSummary` slices by code units: `s.slice(0, room)`. If the cut lands between the two halves of an astral character (emoji, some CJK), the body carries a lone surrogate; `JSON.stringify` emits it as an unpaired escape (`\uD83D`), which strict JSON decoders (GitHub's included) may reject or mojibake — turning the E1 graceful truncation back into a failed stamp.

Requires a >65,535-char summary with an astral character exactly at the boundary, so negligible likelihood today; a one-line guard closes it:

```js
var code = s.charCodeAt(room - 1);
if (code >= 0xD800 && code <= 0xDBFF) room -= 1; // don't split the pair
return s.slice(0, room) + SUMMARY_TRUNCATION_MARKER;
```
